>It gives the output listed at the bottom of the message. Matlab and the
>corresponding C-program on DEC gives  ln(2)=0.69314718055995 and so does the
>IBM Pascal compiler on AIX. Also note that integer powers of 2 should be
>integers (and even numbers).

Remember that a C program will promote the "2" to a double-precision
number, but DEC Pascal only promotes to single-precision.  If you change
the "2" to "2D0" to denote a double-precision literal, you'll get the
answer you desire.

program main(input,output);
var
 i:integer;

begin
 writeln('ln(2)=',ln(2D0):20:18);
 for i:=1 to 40 do
  writeln('i=',i:2,' 2^i=',exp(i*ln(2D0)):10:2);
end.

