> acess by terminal... can someone give me a help... ?

When Enhanced Security is enabled you can set max number of unsuccessful
successive login attempts both for an account and a login-device. In this case
your (pseudo) terminal was locked/disabled.

Use "edauth -dt ...", try to list all terminal entries and look for the one with
"failures#". Delete the whole field (NOT THE ENTRY, just the field between two
":"). Use audit to trrack down the person who did this.

It could be just bad luck, several users trying on the same terminal, for
different accounts. But, you never know.

Nix.



