There is a DSNlink article dated 10 Sep 1998 that describes how to 
vdump/vrestore to a remote tape drive. It is called:

HowTo:Vdump and Vrestore to a Remote System 

Basically pipe the vdump output across the network and use "dd" at the
remote end to write to tape. Command looks something like this:

vdump -0uf - /dir | rsh Host1 -l user dd of=/dev/nrmt0h bs=64k

issued from the system where the disk partition resides. Restoring:

rsh Host1 -l user 'dd if=/dev/nrmt0h bs=64k'| vrestore -x -v -f -

or similar - you should look at the man pages for vdump, dd, vrestore
for any other options that you might need.
Regards,
John Hill

