Hi, 

(note: there is always more than one way to skin the cat)
If this is a new install, edit the disk partition 
table before installing unix. Boot from the operating 
system CD and enter system admin mode/UNIX Shell then 
create the /dev/files for the disk device, 
and then disklabel -re /dev/re??? or /dev/rz???
cd /dev;MAKEDEV re1 or rz1 or whatever the disk is 
called. 

I have recently installed a new multi cpu 4100 with 
many disk array groups and changed the root partition 
to a larger size to allow for future grown, large 
core files, etc, in general we had the space so 
I made the root partition very large. 

Mike

