Chan Kin Man wrote:
> 
> Dear friends,
> 
> I have five digital unix 4.0 AlphaServers. They use a Novell netware as
> the DNS
> server (IP : 168.106.62.21). But, I find that a error message :
> "*** Can't find server name for address 168.106.62.21: Non-existent
> host/domain"
> shown whenever I use nslookup utility.

[SNIP]

> Anyone are kind enough to give me some suggestion ?
> Do I miss some setting on the Digitial Unix?

You are not missing anything on Digital UNIX. The problem is with (Novell) DNS
server. The problem arises from the DNS server being UNABLE to resolve it's own
IP into it's name. I had that problem on Digital UNIX DNS, when I left out the
reverse zone for the DNS itself.

So, the answer is simple, tell your DNS administrator, that they should create
reverse zone for 62.106.168.in-addr.arpa. And if they complain, tell them they
should do it anyway.

The PCs are dumb, so they don't complain about this anomaly.

Nix.



