Since the "official" Y2K ready version is 4.0D, it is a little pointless
to test 3.2C. Digital does have patches to the date commmand for 3.2c,
which are part of their standard patch kit. The patch kit will contain
details on using the century field.
In 4.0D, you can use the formats

date mmddHHMMccyy.ss
date ccyymmddHHMM.ss
date mmddHHMM.ssccyy

to include century specifications, the man page (available on line
in the Digital Unix doc set, start at www.unix.digital.com)
explains how ambiguities are resolved.

See http://www.unix.digital.com/unix/year2000.whitepaper.html for
a discussion of "Compaq's Digital UNIX Year 2000 Readiness". This
explains well other needed feature changes. Note there are a couple of
minor patches since 4.0D that you will need.

