Do you have a specific example?  9 significant digits is more than I'd
expect with single-precision.  The "fast" library doesn't necessarily
give less accurate results than the "accurate" library, especially if
the argument is "reasonable".  The fast library is not as careful in
doing range reductions (not really an issue for ln) and errors may not
get reported properly.

Please also indicate what version of Pascal and DIGITAL UNIX you are
using.



