If your switch tells you it is running half-duplex, you should probably
trust the switch. In any case, with many ethernet card/switch combinations
it is necessary to lock the full-duplex mode on BOTH sides - even if both
pieces of hardware claim to be able to autonegotiate full-duplex. I certainly
have to lock both the tu0 interface in our DPWs and ports on the 3COM 3300
switch to get 100Mbit full-duplex. YMMV.

