Ah. Well, the algorithms are mostly traditional BSD-style
weighted decay blah, blah, blah. There's some proprietary
twists thrown in to smooth out the scheduler's timeshare
behaviors. I don't think you'll be able to find out much more
without sources.

I think what might be seeing is the 2-level priority boost given
to threads blocking in the kernel. Whether this happens or
not is controlled by a kernel variable called, IIRC, give_boost.
I believe you can change it via sysconfigtab, but don't remember what
fields to add and no longer have access to a DU machine. Do
an nm or strings on vmunix and grep for boost for a start.

BTW, that Digital Tech Journal article is at

