: CDs seem to work OK. Ixos is supposed to handle all standard CD formats
: (14 or so), so the question I get from the jukebox installer (I haven't
: touched it myself ;-) is:

: Do Digital use some special CD format which would prevent this working?
: I'm told SUN use Rockwell.

: Anyone have experience doing this kind of thing?

Some of the DU CDs have ISO-9660/Rock Ridge filesystems on them, which 
is the standard for CDs and is very portable between machines.  Others 
have UFS (BSD 4.2 FFS) filesystems, which isn't an impossibly obscure
choice, but it's not really designed to be used on other systems.
Whether your Ixos can deal with them I don't know, but I wouldn't be 
all that surprised if not.

Mark

