Greg Sylvain <gsylvain@mindspring.com> writes:

>I'm trying to port a performance monitoring tool to DU 4.0B that
>monitors NFSv3 performance (among other things), and I can't figure out
>how to get the NFSv3 stats/counts from the kernel akin to nfsstat(1).

>I've run a trace(1) of nfsstat, and it only tells me that, apparently,
>nfsstat makes about 5 msgsnd(2) calls to get this information from the
>kernel  (I assume that this is straight from Mach 2.5 basis ?)

No, nfsstat and all the kernel code is Sun derived.  I suspect the msgsnd
calls are from nlist(3) calls that talk to /sbin/kloadsrv to convert
symbol names to kernel addresses which are then read from /dev/kmem.

The structures involved are not in header files, we may be moving access
to a table(2) someday.  For now, look at kernel names rcstat, clstat,
rsstat, svstat, tcstat and don't tell anyone I posted this.  :-)

Or - parse the output from nfsstat(1).
