You could use dd to take a copy of your boot disk:
e.g. copying from rz0 to rz1
disklabel -z rz1 (if you don't want to keep the disklabel)

dd if=/dev/rrz0c of=/dev/rrz1c skip=16 seek=16 bs=512
This will make a copy of the root disk and also keep the target disk label.
