John Allen (john.allen@geonet-tech.com) wrote:
: Anybody know where I could download a dos2unix/unix2dos
: file conversion set of utilities for Digital Unix?

Download? What do you need to download 'em for?

This is dos2unix:

/bin/sed -e 's/^M$//' -e '$s/^Z//'

This is unix2dos:

/bin/sed -e 's/$/^M/' -e '$a\^J^Z^J'

In both cases, ^M, ^Z, and ^J are corresponding control characters,
which can be entered in vi (and many interactive shells) using the 
Control-V escape. 

Regards,

/Serge.P

P.S. Don't try this in csh, tcsh, or any other shell with broken
apostrophe handling.



