"Seppo.Routimo" wrote:
> 
> Hi
> 
> One curiosity.
> 
> We have a few Alpha-machines with DUnix. Some of them
> have in /etc/fstab
> /proc    /proc    procfs   xx  0 0
> and some
> /proc    /proc    procfs   rw  0 0
> 
> Both seem to work fine. The latter just has one extra
> (ugly 8-) row in df
> 
> Could I put xx in all fstab's or should I change them all rw?

That 4th field in /etc/fstab specifies mount options. The options are:

ro		- Read Only
rw		- Read Write
rq		- R/W + Quota
userquota	- User Quotas apply
groupquota	- Group Quotas apply
sw		- Swap
xx		- to be IGNORED

IOW, if you put "xx", /proc won't be mounted and, thus, won't appear in "df". If
you want to have /proc file system, put "rw".

Nix.
