Well, the "sizer" solution will only work with devices that have support
configured into the kernel.  If no supported is configured, the sizer won't
see it, since sizer just looks inside the kernel and configured drivers.

To use the sizer solution would require the system boot the "genvmunix"
kernel.  Since to do so would require a shutdown and manual reboot, then while
you're there doing the boot, as you suggest, just open the box and look.

