The 3si should be set to postscript

You may have to setup 2 queues in DU 1 for text and the other for
postscript.


1. Configure IP address on Jetdirect Card
2. Add ip address to /etc/hosts file
3. Make sure you can ping the ip address.
4. run the command lprsetup
5. choose add
6. enter the printer name
7. enter remote for the printer type
8. press enter on synonym
9. press enter on the spooler directory ( unless you want it somwhere else)
10. press enter on the error log file
11. enter the hostname you put in the host file for the jetdirect
12. type "text" - for text only printing or "raw" for postscript in the
remote system printer name.
13. enter q on system ?????


You now have a network printer.




