> > mount: Can't load cdfs module
> >
> > With "root" with the same command, it works wothout problem.

The reason why it works for root is that CDFS kernel module *can be loaded
dynamically*. The only problem is that only root has priviliges to load/unload
modules.

In your case, "mount" tried to load the CDFS module, but ran out of priviliges.

The best thing is the suggestion above, from Kurt. But I'm not exactly sure what
is DU's view of ordinary user mounting a file system. UFS, for instance, can be
mounted only by root.

Nix.



