Sorry for answering so late, but other things had higher priority :-)
Maybe dop is not documented, because it is normally used internally by
the CDE (?).

The dop config file is /etc/doprc
New commands are added with dop -a fullpathofcommand
commands are removed with dop -d commandname
e.g. dop -a /usr/sbin/adduser
     dop -d removeuser

Authorized users have to be inserted by hand into /etc/doprc
e.g. 

adduser{
  {users { jones smith }}
  {path { /usr/sbin/adduser }}
}

Look into that file for more examples.
Commands are executed e.g. from account smith by calling:
	/usr/sbin/dop adduser


Yes, I read the comment from Ed Wensel III
(Ed Wensell III aka THE StormRaiser <ewensell@pstcc.cc.tn.us.net>)
My opinion: Every command with suid bit is insecure somehow. I don't
think that sudo has no security holes.

