For anyone having problems with handling the BackSpace key correctly on
Digital Unix 4.0d in the default X11/CDE environment and in particular
getting it to work consistently in multiple applications such as Netscape
Navigator 4.5, Applixware 4.41, tcl/tk apps etc then cop this!

xmodmap -e "keysym BackSpace = BackSpace Delete"

If you place this wherever you want it eg
/etc/dt/config/Xsession.d/{scriptname} then all users will benefit upon next
login.	I got the inspiration for this from a Linux newsgroup where the guy
said it worked for him the other way around ie Delete before BackSpace and he
used keycodes instead of keysyms but I couldn't get it working in my
environment until I swapped the BackSpace and Delete references as above. 
Now all apps responds correctly to BackSpace and Applixware has even learned
how to correctly handle the Del key (but only in the Send Mail window!!).

Tyson Ackland
ONA/IT

