I added the following to my .Xdefaults file

!-----------------------------------------------
*defaultVirtualBindings:\n\
        osfBackSpace    :       <key>Delete\n
!-----------------------------------------------

This seems to do the trick for me in all X-Windows apps so far.

I also included the following to get the arrow keys to work in edit
boxes

!-----------------------------------------------------
*defaultVirtualBindings:\n\
        osfBackSpace    :       <key>Delete     \n\
        osfLeft         :       <key>Left       \n\
        osfRight        :       <key>Right      \n\
        osfUp           :       <key>Up         \n\
        osfDown         :       <key>Down       \n
!-----------------------------------------------------

Again, this is just some stuff that I either learned from someone else,
or I experimented with it until it did what I wanted for me.  Maybe it
will do similar things for someone else.



