You can't even do a straight shot from 3.2 to 4.0x let alone from 3.0
(unless you want to start all over from the ground up). First thing to
do is to check out the docs starting with 3.2 and go from there if they
are on hand. The 4.0x doc sets only provide an upgrade path from 3.2c on
up. Check out:

http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/pub_page/doc_list.html

If you do not have the hard copies...

Anyway, if you are lucky the upgrade path should look like:

3.0b ?->? 3.2c -> 4.0 ?->? 4.0e

Each update takes around 1.5 to 3 hours depending on machine speed and
layered products. Hopefully there aren't many more steps between 3.0b ->
3.2c and 4.0 -> 4.0e (the online 3.0 docs are only in PostScript which I
didn't want to spend time printing, and the 4.0e are actually the
un-updated 4.0b set... Go fig).

To make things more interesting, most of the Y2K fixes are in 4.0d and
above... Have fun! :)
-- 

Until soon...
