I did the same path a few monthd ago, just form 3.2a or such.  I *think*
I went to 3.2g or such before going to 4.0a and then 4.0d.  Be very thorough
checking that you can do what you intend to do, though I think the upgrade
sw checks for you, and won't let you do an upgrade you can't.

Now, there is a BIG problem I ran into.  My disk was too small.  The root
disk needs went up a bit going to 4.0a from 3.2x, and regardless how
much I tried to cut down on unnneeded stuff, it would not fit. I was about
100 KB within the goal when I had to give up, after spending about 2-3 hrs
on this. You can't cheat and delete things it puts back on again ;-)

So make sure you have room.  I ended up stealing an unused 4 GB disk from
another machine, and that did it.  The old disk was a 2 GB disk, I believe.

I found it took about 2-3 hrs to do each step (not counting the slimming
down process). I had only done one upgrade before that day.

You might also contact the vendor to see if their product works on DUX
4.0x.  I have an old version of Progress on HP-UX 10, it was originally made
for 9.x, and it works, but I was fortunate that I could test it out on another
10.x system in advance. 


Steen


