>I want to use AltaVista Firewall on an OSF/1 machine with 2 FDDI
>interfaces and 1 100baseT interface.  Will an AlphaServer 800 have
>the horsepower to be an adequate firewall?  I'll have about 200
>hosts behind the firewall and probably not a whole lot of
>internet traffic.
>
>---Matt

It depends on what you mean by "probably not a whole lot of internet traffic." 
If you have a lot of people web browsing or one or two people doing massive
and/or numerous ftp downloads, it could be kinda slow even with a 500MHz CPU
(the fastest an AS800 can handle).  If your 200 hosts don't communicate much
with the outside world, there'll be no performance hit due to the firewall
machine at all.  You might have to tweak the OS as well (see
http://www.unix.digital.com/internet/tuning.html) Hope this helps.


