Steve Hamilton wrote in message <36DC1E20.EACF90C3@mddc.com>...
>Please, forgive my ignorance in advance.
>
>I have taken over a server running OSF 3.0b.  My predecessor never
>upgraded the OS.  We have every release Digital put out, and none of
>them are installed.
>
>My question is, can I upgrade from OSF to Digital Unix v4.0e directly or
>must I install each and every upgrade?
>
>My main concern is that our mission critical software is running on
>Progress Version 6, and I cannot afford to have it delayed more than
>about 1/2 a day.
>
Well, You will need a few intermediate steps to do that upgrade, from you
will need at least four or five intermediate steps to do this, so I think
half a day is a little optimistic.

Lots of issues here so hold on tight.

Year 2000 issues will probably mean you have a short timescale for this
upgrade (that deadline will not move)

I believe that there is a license issue with going from a 3.x system to a
4.x system (You need to have a support contract for the upgrade to be
legal?? something like that anyway.)

I wonder if your mission critical application will work on 4.0e ?

I wonder if progress V6 will run ?


I think your best bet will be to rent a similar system, Install your
application on it, test it as much as you can in isolation, then use your
half day of downtime to transfer the system to your production kit.

If this is not possible, quit ;-)










